From 754313462607b6e1a90d9ba484794fce1a283008 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yomathnotcool <125728853+DengZhiyuan-math@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 16:13:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix: the Reader runs under proof-cli's reader role and writes
 the full bibliography (#20)

The Reader's environment sets PROOF_AGENT_ROLE=reader (proof-cli#203), and
its permissions allow `proof node create *`: proof-cli refuses kind=claim,
--parent and --reassign on the parsed arguments, so the raw `claim "`
patterns go and a statement quoting it is written.

The ban on `reference import --identifier/--source-type` and the brief's
"leave out" line go too: under ADR-0022 (proof-cli#199) a Trust rule covers
only the researcher's imports, so the Reader's import still reads unreviewed
under a matching rule.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
